{
  "id": "xKa2mcqpLlhoTlTU",
  "name": "WF-05a Recovery Approval",
  "description": "Onward Phase 6: the single human-approval entry point. Validates the plan exists, belongs to the incident, is feasible, and has not already been decided, then records an explicit approved/rejected decision and (only on approval) fires WF-05 execution fire-and-forget.",
  "active": true,
  "note": "Published and live-gate-tested (Phase 6, hardened Phase 7). Real webhook: POST https://raiha-mariam.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/recovery-approval. Phase 7 red-team finding and fix: two truly-concurrent approval requests for the same plan both passed the pre-insert 'Already Decided?' check, so the loser hit the real approvals.plan_id unique-constraint violation with no onError handling -- the whole workflow crashed with a raw n8n error instead of a clean response. Fixed by giving both Insert Approval Approved and Insert Approval Rejected onError:continueErrorOutput, routing failures to a shared Refetch Approval After Conflict -> Found After Approval Conflict? step, and responding with the same 409 already_decided shape the sequential-duplicate path already uses (or a genuine 500 only if the row still isn't found after refetch). Verified live with 3 truly-concurrent approval requests for one plan: before the fix, 2 of 3 crashed with a raw 'Error in workflow'; after, all 3 respond cleanly (one 200 approved, two 409 already_decided), and exactly one approvals row exists. Also added retryOnFail (3 tries, 1s wait) to every Supabase read/write per CLAUDE.md §14, after a live transient Supabase 504 on a downstream node (WF-05's Fetch Approval) was found to crash a run with zero trace -- the same class of gap existed here. Proven live: approval of a feasible plan -> approvals row + audit_log 'plan_approved' + WF-05 triggered; rejection -> approvals row decision='rejected' + audit_log 'plan_rejected' + zero rows in execution_runs/execution_actions/work_orders; approval attempt on an infeasible plan -> HTTP 422 'plan_infeasible', zero rows in approvals/execution_runs for that incident.",
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "availableInMCP": true
  },
